Linux files used by the illumos DRM port

Upstream: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git
Version: v7.2
Commit: 8d3ae59288f1e7d58d76558a6ee96d533bc5019f
Pin record: usr/src/uts/intel/io/i915n/PIN

The build reads this tree directly. Port changes are commits on these files;
edit a vendored file and commit it on the integration branch. Its git log
records the port history. linux-pristine holds only pristine imports and
their metadata; merge it to bring upstream changes into the port.

The initial selection is the normalized union of the i915 display, i915
headless and drm_kms linux-inputs.txt lists at illumos-drm
e101f9814da43756bc7f13f02ae6020f05e7d069, with .illumos/mit-include mapped
to include/, six GPL originals excluded, and fourteen build-script inputs
added (five header copies and nine licence-generation fallback headers).
The two unmodified helper C files, drm_mm.c and drm_cache.c, were added by
a second pristine import; their two headers were already present. Their
old helper patch series were empty. Builds stage just these four helper
files to preserve the helpers' include selection and compiler flags.

SOURCES has 849 upstream paths with pristine SHA-256 and licence class,
separated by tabs. All are SPDX MIT, a dual licence offering MIT, or an
MIT/HPND permission notice. Original notices remain. .gitattributes disables
Git text conversion throughout this directory to preserve source bytes.

Six port headers are separate MIT stand-ins, not imports of GPL originals:
  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_trace.h
  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/intel_uncore_trace.h
  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_trace.h
  drivers/gpu/drm/drm_trace.h
  drivers/platform/x86/intel_ips.h
  drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology_internal.h
The first four are committed outputs of usr/src/uts/intel/io/i915n/illumos/gen-trace-stubs.py;
the last two originate in this repository's MIT headers. They have no upstream
SOURCES record. Their GPL originals are never imported. No GPL-only file is
vendored. The normal build runs none of the maintainer generators.

Verify without an upstream checkout or a fetched tree:
  sh usr/src/contrib/linux/verify-vendored.sh -n
This requires a SOURCES record for every upstream source, exactly the six
stand-ins above, no symlinks, and acceptance of every source by the existing
usr/src/uts/intel/io/i915n/check-licences.py gate. Only .gitattributes, SOURCES, README and
verify-vendored.sh are excluded as metadata/tooling. The licence gate checks
the first 6000 characters and first 60 lines for an SPDX MIT alternative
(rejecting AND/WITH), or an MIT/HPND permission notice.

Optional -p /path/to/full/linux verifies every pristine digest against Git
objects of the pinned upstream revision. Repeat -i /path/to/linux-inputs.txt
to check build inputs. Without -n, supply a prepared Linux tree as the last
argument for byte comparison, including its old mit-include header copies;
this mode retains the import's comparison with the former fetch model.

To update Linux, regenerate the input selection and SOURCES at the new pin,
import only pristine MIT-compatible files on linux-pristine, then merge
that branch into the integration branch and review conflicts with port
commits. Update PIN, this README and verify-vendored.sh's upstream_rev.
Regenerate the six stand-ins and configuration outputs from the full pinned
upstream checkout. gen-trace-stubs.py, usr/src/uts/intel/io/i915n/config/gen-config.py
and usr/src/uts/intel/io/i915n/illumos/gen-nodisplay.py are maintainer tools for this step;
the latter two take the full checkout as their tree argument. Commit the
outputs and repeat provenance/licence, build-input and native build checks.
